Seaside of house

Seaside of house, there is a large stone terrace with some chairs and a table with a broken kite on. The house has many windows, and a balcony on the upper floor. From an overhead tree branch hangs a large bell. I can go around the house south or north, or down the stairs towards the sea. There is a large double door leading into the living room but it is crawling with big ants.
On the terrace there is some paper.
> south

> south

South of house

 This is a very peaceful side of the house, shielded from the wind from the north. Us kids seldom come here. Grandma grows her roses here: beautiful large stands of rhododendron. They smell wonderful! I could imagine lingering here for a while.
I can continue round the house east towards the sea or west back to the front entrance. I can also explore the woods to the south.
> look under roses

> look under roses
Looking in the darkness under the roses I can see something. After some time I realise: This is a large weed cutter. There used to be weeds around here but not anymore. Someone forgot to put the tool away.
> take weed cutter

> take weed cutter
I pick it up.
> east

> east

Seaside of house

Seaside of house, there is a large stone terrace with some chairs and a table with a broken kite on. The house has many windows, and a balcony on the upper floor. From an overhead tree branch hangs a large bell. I can go around the house south or north, or down the stairs towards the sea. There is a large double door leading into the living room but it is crawling with big ants.
On the terrace there is some paper.
