South point

There is a serene kind of beauty here, with trees thinning out towards the glittering sea. I can see a pair of swans with their young ones, not caring about my presence, feeding by the shore. The trunks reflect the sunlight filtered through the foliage. There are several stones scattered on the ground among the pine cones. It is dead quiet. What am i doing here? Why am I here? This is so peaceful I could fall asleep. Of course I must not. The truth of this paradise is that it is boring.
There is absolutely nothing to do.

The only way from here is north towards the house. Some piece of white cloth is hanging from a narrow branch. I cannot reach it.
> throw stone at trunks

> throw stone at trunks
I pick a stone and throw it at a tree. It misses by some margin. I think I could hit it after some practise.
> throw stone at trunks

> throw stone at trunks
I throw another stone at the same tree and now it is a very near miss.
> throw stone at trunks

> throw stone at trunks
This time I hit the tree with a resounding thud. My aim is not off!
> throw stone at white cloth

> throw stone at white cloth
I pick up a stone and take careful aim. I throw it and it is a perfect hit! The white cloth disentangles from the branch and flutters to the ground.
> take towel

> take towel
