Stairs

The broad stairs connect the house with the sea. Close to the house they are made of solid stone blocks, further down they are a bit smaller and made of concrete. I can go up to the house or down to the foot of a long pier. I can also go south to the majestic vista that projects high over the sea.
> down

> down

Foot of pier

Here the long pier runs from the beach out into the sea. I can go out on it, or up the stairs toward the house. On either side (north and south) are small beaches I can try.
> out

> out
I think I can go out on the pier. I heard the kids are out there swimming.

On the pier

The pier is very long and now I am in the middle of it. There is water on both sides. I can go out towards the sea or in towards the house.
> out

> out

End of pier

Pier end. The kids are swimming here, having a lot of fun in the water, and want me to join!
The way from here is in towards land. There is a small boat tied to the pier.
> swim

> swim
Finally it is time! I drop all my stuff and undress. The kids beckon. I stand at the edge of the pier. There is a small ladder where I can climb in and out of the water but it is much more fun to jump. So I jump, shouting wildly and waving my arms.

The water is ice cold and hits me with a shock. I scramble for the surface but it's hard, the waves are quite high. I can barely touch the bottom, and I don't think I can swim, at least not in these waves and this cold water. I look around for the kids but cannot see anybody.

How come I am in the water all alone? This is a nightmare, I seriously start getting cold. I tiptoe towards the ladder, swinging my arms in a kind of swimming motion, with mixed results. Then a large wave hits me and propels me forward.

I reach the ladder and manage to hold on to it as another wave passes. Then I laboriously climb the ladder to stand on the pier, shivering uncontrollably of the cold. For some time I am frozen still and then realise that I need to get warm quickly.

I start towelling fiercely to get dry, but that does not stop the cold. I put my clothes back on and start running towards the house. I am like the wind, unstoppable and without thoughts. In no time I get to the foot of the pier and continue up the stairs, and run into the living room, where grandma is waiting for me in her armchair.

I fling myself into her warm embrace and for some time I just sit there, feeling the warmth return. It seems like an eternity. I could sit here forever and enjoy the soft warm bliss. Grandma keeps saying soothing words. But of course nothing lasts forever.

We stand up.
- Wait here, I'll get you something nice to eat to get your spirits up, grandma says. She goes into the dining room and I hear her entering the kitchen. I hear her unlocking and opening the pantry. She rummages there a bit and then returns with a cookie.
- Eat this and you'll feel better in no time, she says, and disappears into the house.
------------
I do feel better after eating the cookie. In fact I feel completely restored.

And I never heard her close the pantry.

