I worm my way upwards and finally emerge in a cavern.

Cavern

I am in a surprisingly large cavern. The walls and ceiling consist of stone blocks of varying sizes. It takes a while for my eyes to adjust to the dim light. It is quite cold.

Finally I can take it all in. The cavern is almost empty. Perhaps there were treasures here once but someone beat me to it. Perhaps a long time ago. I can see traces of digging where the floor has been disturbed. Now there is nothing left. Then the realisation hits me: I am inside the mound. The great mound of Gilleholmen! Now I have uncovered its secrets. Or at least some of them. Who built it, what was in here, and who plundered it? This I will probably never know.
The plunderers must have left in a hurry, because I can see a torch half buried  in the floor.
The only way out is going down into the crawlway.
In the ceiling, just beyond my reach, is a small crack between two stones letting in some light from the outside.
